  "summary_en": "Japanese ministerial ordinance implementing Article 99-3 of the Road Transport Vehicle Act, setting a permit system for specified modifications of vehicles via program changes (e.g., over-the-air software updates), requiring operators to be certified for cybersecurity and program management capability and to comply with safety standards.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Permit required for software-based modifications altering vehicle device performance, done via telecommunications or media distribution",
   "Applicants need MLIT capability certificates for cybersecurity and program management, valid three years",
   "Permits granted per modified vehicle or vehicle type, with application documents and safety standard conformity proof",
   "Permit holders must report changes, keep records, and take cybersecurity measures specified by notice",
   "Effective 23 November 2020; currently amended through 2026"
